# CLAUDE.md — {{APP_NAME}}

{{ONE_LINE_DESCRIPTION}} HTTP service. Bun · Hono · TypeScript (strict) ·
`bun test` · oxlint + oxfmt. Read this file first — it is the map and the rulebook.

## Repo map

```
src/app.ts       The Hono app — routes + middleware are mounted here (wiring only)
src/index.ts     Server entry — Bun.serve(app.fetch) on the validated PORT
src/routes/      One module per resource — thin HTTP handlers, no business logic
src/services/    Business logic — framework-agnostic, unit-testable
src/utilities/   Shared pure helpers (dates, formatters, …)
src/constants/   env.ts (hand-validated) + enums
src/types/       Cross-cutting TS types
.github/workflows/  CI gate (type-check · lint · format · test)
```

Each `src/*` folder has its own `README.md` listing what lives there — read it
before adding files, and add a line when you add something notable.

## Tooling

- Use `bun` for everything (`bun install`, `bun run <script>`, `bunx <bin>`,
  `bun test`). Bun loads `.env` natively — no dotenv.
- `bun run dev` runs the server with hot reload (`bun --hot src/index.ts`).
- `bun run check` runs the full gate: type-check + lint + format-check +
  structure-check + test.
- `bun run lint:fix` and `bun run fmt` auto-fix.
- Pre-commit (Lefthook) runs oxlint + oxfmt on staged files.
- Tests run non-interactively via `bun test` (config in `bunfig.toml`).

## Gate — run before every push

`bun run check` = all five, in order; each must exit 0:

```bash
bun run type-check      # tsc --noEmit (strict)
bun run lint            # oxlint --deny-warnings
bun run fmt:check       # oxfmt --check
bun run check:structure # bash scripts/check-structure.sh — folder-tree rules
bun run test            # bun test
```

## Blocked patterns (the gate rejects these — not just review)

Structure is **machine-enforced**: oxlint carries `no-restricted-imports` (barrel +
deep-relative imports), `unicorn/filename-case` (kebab-case), and `max-lines`
(300 code lines); `scripts/check-structure.sh` checks the folder tree itself
(allowed `src/` dirs, per-folder READMEs, no stray `index.ts`).

- `as any`, `: any`, `as unknown as T` → use `unknown` + type guards.
- `console.log`, `debugger` → use `console.warn` / `console.error` or the logger.
- **Barrel files** (an `index.ts` that only re-exports, or importing one) → import
  the concrete file. Only `src/index.ts` (the server entry) may be named `index.ts`.
- **Deep relative imports** (`../../x`) → use the `@/` alias.
- **Unexpected `src/` layout** → only `routes services utilities constants types`
  (each with a `README.md`) + `app.ts`/`index.ts` at the root. Adding an
  integration dir (`db`, `middleware`) means adding it to `allowed_dirs` in
  `scripts/check-structure.sh`.
- Files over 300 code lines (tests exempt) → split.
- Tests outside a sibling `__tests__/` (review).
- Schema libraries app-wide (`zod`, `yup`, …) for env / general parsing → env and
  external data are validated by hand (type guards on `unknown`).

## Conventions

- **Path alias**: `@/*` → `src/*`. Always import via alias — never deep relative
  paths like `../../services/x`.
- **Filenames**: kebab-case, named after the export (`health-service.ts` →
  `getHealth`; `user-route.ts` → the user router). One primary export per file.
- **Named exports** everywhere — no default exports.
- **Routes are thin**: a route module parses the request, calls a service, and
  shapes the response. No business logic, no direct DB access in routes.
- **Services hold logic**: framework-agnostic functions in `src/services/`,
  unit-testable without spinning up the server.
- **One route module per resource**; mount it in `src/app.ts`.
- **Validation**: env + external input validated by hand (type guards on
  `unknown`) — no schema library app-wide. If you opt into request validation,
  keep it at the boundary (route level) only.
- **Errors**: never swallow. Propagate or map to an HTTP response; no `any`, no
  non-null assertions.
- **Doc line required**: every module and public symbol carries a concise
  `/** … */` one-liner. Brief, but not optional.
- **Docs in sync**: a change to any user-facing surface (a route, its behavior,
  env vars, commands, config) updates the prose that describes it — README,
  folder READMEs, this file — in the same change.
- **Commits**: `type(scope): description` (conventional). Push to feature
  branches; never directly to main.

## Testing

- Colocate tests in a sibling `__tests__/` (`health-service.ts` →
  `__tests__/health-service.test.ts`); keep the test tree flat.
- Real data, no mock-data tests. Exercise routes end-to-end with
  `app.request('/path')` and assert on the real response; test services with real
  inputs. A test that only proves a mock echoes its own setup is banned.

## Stack additions

Integrations are opt-in (DB client, bearer-token auth middleware, pino logging).
When you add one, follow `LIBRARIES.md` from the kit and document it under the
relevant `src/*/README.md`.
